{'name':'Rosencrantz and Guildenstern','role':'Hamlet’s old friends','description':'Summoned by the king and queen to keep Hamlet company and discover the cause of his change. Friendship and service to the court come to pull in different directions.'},
{'name':'Fortinbras','role':'Prince of Norway','description':'Nephew of Norway’s present king and son of the Fortinbras defeated by the old King Hamlet. His military plans give the Danish court’s conflict an external setting.'},
{'name':'The players, gravediggers, and Osric','role':'Other important voices','description':'The players display the force of emotion and performance. The gravediggers joke about death, rank, and law. The courtier Osric’s elaborate speech immediately invites Hamlet’s mockery.'}
